{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other","id":1419691,"title":"Running Scion Online - Roll20 vs Astral vs Other","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-22T18:59:38-07:00","id":1419691,"title":"Running Scion Online - Roll20 vs Astral vs Other","content":"I plan to run <b>Scion</b> game in coming weeks on <b>Discord</b>. However, from my previous RPG online experience, action ( and combat) heavy games are best supported by the VTTRPG platforms. So question is simple - <b>What online RPG platform is best for Scion?</b> I mention Roll20 and Astral as those are seems most supported by the Onyx Path by products, in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-11-2020, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T21:30:06-07:00","id":1419711,"title":"","content":"I run Scion with a dicebot on Discord. If you want to be elaborate you should probably make a dedicated server with subchannels for IC, OOC, and using things like Channel Descriptions to keep track of the Momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:26:05-07:00","id":1419769,"title":"","content":"There is a character sheet template on Roll20 for Scion 2e. I haven't used it. So I can't speak to how good it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:56:23-07:00","id":1419775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1419769#post1419769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a character sheet template on Roll20 for Scion 2e. I haven't used it. So I can't speak to how good it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty good and gives you plenty of room to write down and contain your Birthrights / Purviews as well as other info about your character. I prefer it to the official pen and paper character sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T07:58:12-07:00","id":1419786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1419775#post1419775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty good and gives you plenty of room to write down and contain your Birthrights / Purviews as well as other info about your character. I prefer it to the official pen and paper character sheets.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Does it also contains Antagonists templates?</b> I had the problem in running <b>CoD</b> on Roll20 that I could not written enemies with different stats than PCs. Needed to do my own homebrew template then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-23-2020, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T08:46:07-07:00","id":1419794,"title":"","content":"Since the antagonist stat blocks are pretty small, you could use the GM notes section on a token to list the pools and powers. You wouldn't have the click to roll functionality of a template, but it's a workaround.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T09:34:31-07:00","id":1419802,"title":"","content":"Roll20 has been great for centralising player's character sheets and those rare occasions when I want to actually map something, but I do tend to use it alongside a word doc with everything else (e.g. antagonists) in. Also we use skype instead of the built-in video chat. But yeah, there's plenty of GM notes fields or you could make handouts that are only visible to you. Also, the sheets do 10-again automatically but if you're rolling raw in the chat remember the exclamation mark /r {Xd10<b>!</b>}&gt;8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","name":"CassieCataria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T10:10:52-07:00","id":1419806,"title":"","content":"We play Scion on Roll20 for the dice, sheets and handouts.<br /> <br /> Also for some drawing and references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T13:53:06-07:00","id":1421051,"title":"","content":"My big problem with Roll20 is it doesn't allow you to say that you are &quot;Playing&quot; Scion, so you can't advertise your game very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","user":"Geomancer","date":". 10-30-2020, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T20:48:15-08:00","id":1423174,"title":"","content":"Are there in <b>Scion</b> something like Speed trait, like is in <b>CoD</b>? I ask, because when using <b>Roll20</b> and similar platforms maps, I need to decide on shape and scale of 1 movement unit on map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-11-2020, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T23:18:36-08:00","id":1423190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423174#post1423174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there in <b>Scion</b> something like Speed trait, like is in <b>CoD</b>? I ask, because when using <b>Roll20</b> and similar platforms maps, I need to decide on shape and scale of 1 movement unit on map.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, there is no such thing. <br /> <br /> If you decide that a character will have difficulty getting to a slightly distant place and doing something else in one round then you can have them do a Mixed Action with Athletics + Dexterity or Might, or just let them skip a combat round or two while they sprint towards where they must be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T23:56:25-08:00","id":1423200,"title":"","content":"Are there Range Bands in <b>Scion</b>? Maybe limit working distance in round to Short or Medium one then? &lt; Looks into his books &gt; Oh, here it is...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://previews.dropbox.com/p/thumb/AA8MRFC4fXHMXs5qgPLO1_25MVE9a1tZYBzoohgZPV2rzKczrvRgNWcJthGRUtFTmwxYIkp9AG63gKHoHNXd8BaaX2AfZ9mZQJ62RwltiurBYyhKSzy5bc_WQA9dP7K-ukekbwt10jfqmNMn9N7AlyDAY5-GQz_YsohVcOiFE0SjDJuN3ZlrD7Ra8UsPO8dfkeNKswZZkLXuiDPx5jW1IzB1KZowAZo5TPbKpuaGiA7ZT0EC5NdvJ9U1tzPwfOFl7WSjnjPy78MGs-WbK4fvBJmpBB5wq3wtrTus3ONX5y0ai5HQk1-vNgZkEtxDvqA9GFd9OWosiL1DgUDTgWmSPWSD889VIssXHFvZZHc8Gk74hA/p.png?size=1280x960&amp;size_mode=3\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So if Short is 3 to 30 meters - I suspect making <b>unit scale as to 1 meter and approximate to CoD standard of 10 m Speed per turn</b> for character will be fine. Rolling Athletics + Dexterity or Might will get double on that, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T05:21:08-08:00","id":1423242,"title":"","content":"The closest thing to a speed trait is Speed Scale. In Hero, that would probably involve a Boon or invoking your legend as the fastest person alive, or whatever your title might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T08:17:47-08:00","id":1423277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423242#post1423242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing to a speed trait is Speed Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well, I just hack it then for use to play on Roll20 maps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just giving Speed 10 for all characters not pointed as having different Speed than humans. Then giving Speed Scale would be like normal Speed x 2 or x 3, between Scale points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T12:56:38-08:00","id":1423345,"title":"","content":"I would (and always do) discourage using exact meterage for Scion. I honestly wouldn't recommend using a battle grid of any sort.<br /> <br /> Like, example: What is 'Short range' for a human?<br /> <br /> Now, what's 'Short range' for a giant?<br /> <br /> See?<br /> <br /> Don't think of Short Range as '3-30 meters', think of Short Range as 'Too far to stab immediately, but if I lunge and THEN stab I can do it'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T14:04:05-08:00","id":1423365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423345#post1423345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, what's 'Short range' for a giant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are not Giants have - by definition - Size Scale to make their Ranges larger?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423345#post1423345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would (and always do) discourage using exact meterage for Scion. I honestly wouldn't recommend using a battle grid of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>So use <i>only</i> Discord then and 'Mind's Eye' of yours. I do like tactical fights, from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T15:11:21-08:00","id":1423385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423365#post1423365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are not Giants have - by definition - Size Scale to make their Ranges larger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Size Scale doesn't make Range Bands longer. It's just that &quot;Bigger things have bigger size ranges&quot;<br /> <br /> Size <b>Scale</b> gives Enhancement on certain actions, because Scale is a mechanic. What is Short range for a Giant may be Medium for a human, but that's not a function of Scale.<br /> <br /> And you can get VERY tactical in Scion. Just not in the way a Battle Grid in any way helps. Scion has no flanking mechanics, no real benefit for positioning, no real need to count out exact meterage.<br /> <br /> Tactical fights in Scion will be less &quot;So if our Loki Scion moves here then we can get a +1 Enhancement Flanking bonus from their Sneak Attack&quot;, it will be &quot;So we'll let our Scion of Persephone go first, and she'll use that Fertility Boon to give the Giant cancer of the everything, which will negate his bonus successes from his Scale. After that we can have our Zeus Scion use a Blessing on our Durga Scion, who then makes a killshot with their bow.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T22:18:55-08:00","id":1423470,"title":"","content":"I run Scion on Roll20 but it's largely just because of the sheets and the dice rollers. They allow everything to be easily stored within the game, along with fun images. The game isn't really built for set out grids. That's largely best left to theatre of the mind. Whereas D&amp;D and similar games make 'where you are on the grid' tactically important, yeah, Kyman's pretty much nailed it on the head in the previous post about what Scion tactics largely look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T05:23:46-08:00","id":1423526,"title":"","content":"I run TC:Aeon on Roll20, and I use the screen mostly to show a picture I stole off the internet to represent the place they're at and to move tokens in and out of a box to represent the momentum pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T05:46:09-08:00","id":1423534,"title":"","content":"I play Scion and run Trinity Continuum on Roll20 mainly to have a place to hold all sheets and roll the dice (sometimes draw some references), as we use Discord to do all the rest (talk, send images and hand outs).<br /> <br /> It works fine, even with a simple Scion sheet to handle all the kinds of characters (so far, Origin, Heroes, Talents and Novas).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T14:31:03-08:00","id":1423830,"title":"","content":"One good use I have of the screen in Roll20 is to put up lists of the different Stunts available in combat as well as the options for Marvels. That has helped my players do their combat rounds quicker and smoother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T14:42:38-08:00","id":1423835,"title":"","content":"Having a visual representation of the momentum and tension pool using tokens helped alot as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T15:31:01-08:00","id":1423852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423830#post1423830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One good use I have of the screen in Roll20 is to put up lists of the different Stunts available in combat as well as the options for Marvels. That has helped my players do their combat rounds quicker and smoother.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423835#post1423835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a visual representation of the momentum and tension pool using tokens helped alot as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, how do you do those!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Stunts list as Handout or Macros? How to put Momentum as physical tokens in Roll20? Very cool things you propose here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T16:14:33-08:00","id":1423869,"title":"","content":"I found image for plain circles (gold for momentum and black for tension) then i have them as tokens on the &quot;board&quot;.<br /> Playing physically on a table i would definitely use tokens (or dices) to show the pools as well since i found it helps alot for the players to see the points in the pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T22:31:24-08:00","id":1423938,"title":"","content":"The list of stunts was nothing special, I just made text boxes on the Roll20 screen and wrote down the Stunts for Close Combat, Ranged, Throwing etc. It was tedious but worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T23:38:56-08:00","id":1423943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423938#post1423938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just made text boxes on the Roll20 screen and wrote down the Stunts for Close Combat, Ranged, Throwing etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this one hack? <a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/forum/post/4376302/formatting-text-boxes\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/forum/post/43...ing-text-boxes</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T00:04:55-08:00","id":1423952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423943#post1423943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like this one hack? <a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/forum/post/4376302/formatting-text-boxes\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/forum/post/43...ing-text-boxes</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though I put the text in boxes of different colors to make them easier on the eye.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T09:56:04-08:00","id":1424296,"title":"","content":"I've been running Scion in roll20 and the sheet someone made for it is great for PC's.<br /> <br /> The sheet has a spot for Momentum, but since that is a shared resource between everyone I just use a token for Momentum that everyone can update.<br /> <br /> When using Momentum the sheet doesn't have a way to add dice to a roll, so we either find a Skill + Attribute combo that adds up the size of the pool we want, or roll a second time for Momentum.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Storyguide characters I found it helpful to create the four antagonist templates, then I make a copy and rename things when I'm building individual antagonists.<br /> <br /> I used the Attributes &amp; Abilities tab and added Abilities for their dice pools. I created an Ability for their Primary, Secondary, Desperation, and Initiative pool. I also added an Attribute for Health.<br /> <br /> This is the macro I used for their Abilities<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&amp;{template:default} {{name=Foe}} {{Primary Pool=[[{7d10!10}&gt;8]]}}</div>You can change the name and names of the roll, so for a real antagonist it would look like<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&amp;{template:default} {{name=Elatus}} {{Magic, Scheming=[[{9d10!10}&gt;8]]}}</div>Be careful about accidently deleting a { when updating the names, the roll will probably work but the formatting gets all wonky.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you click the 'Show as Token Action' checkbox for an Ability you can see their pools as buttons you can press when you have the token selected. So you can just click on the antagonist, see the names of their pools, and hit a button.<br /> <br /> I'm not super good with the roll20 macros, so I just eyeball Enhancement and add it to the roll afterwards (or as is often the case, forget to).<br /> <br /> When you click on one of the buttons to roll it'll show the name of the antagonist and the successes. It doesn't know how to handle a botch, but it will flag the result in red if there are 1's in the roll. So a 0 with a red border means a botch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this helps! I've found it really easy to manage antagonists like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T10:49:40-08:00","id":1424309,"title":"","content":"I'm tinkering on the Roll20 sheet to make fork of it, with Antagonists section added. I only need to resolve the hiding part, to cover Antagonists section on PCs variants - and show it on Antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:41:52-08:00","id":1424371,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Yeah, I'd say the big wants would be an option for Antagonists, and a way to add extra dice to a player roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T17:24:39-08:00","id":1424391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1423365#post1423365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So use <i>only</i> Discord then and 'Mind's Eye' of yours. I do like tactical fights, from time to time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's fine, but Scion really doesn't support it. Fights are narrative by design, you won't find any references to specific rules for distance, time, reach, positioning, any of that stuff. The game very literally does not care where you are on a field and largely only includes the very abstract range bands to illustrate why it might be easier to shoot a character that's narratively described as being very far away rather than trying to stab them with a sword.<br /> <br /> If you really, really want to use a map of some kind for your game, I would recommend zone maps. Rather than making a precise map of a location, just have several areas on the board that convey the general environment, any Arenas associated with each one, and how they connect to one another.<br /> <br /> So for example if you were having a divine martial arts tournament, where some of the players were competing atop bamboo poles over a bed of spikes, and some were in the stands full of screaming fans, with a cage separating them. You wouldn't map out every detail of both. Rather you would designate an &quot;Arena&quot; zone, outlined that it has the arena condition that meant that everyone had to keep balance to avoid falling onto the spikes, a &quot;Stands&quot; zone, outlined that navigating through it could be difficult given the frenzied fans, and designate that anyone trying to cross from the arena to the stands will have to deal with the cage separating the two.<br /> <br /> But obviously this can all just be extrapolated in mind's eye instead, because Divine Demigods typically don't care about something as fiddly as how many feet they move in the span of 6 seconds, they get where they're going whenever is most dramatically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T17:44:08-08:00","id":1424395,"title":"","content":"In my games, we hardly use anything more than a map as reference (we just mark which room or close to what the characters are) and we more than once used the Arena idea. It worked fine both to separate different floors in a bar and for a fight happening around and inside a fountain, including tests to move from one area to the other as part of a complex action (just moving had no test).<br /> <br /> Worked very well in my opinion and saved us of moving all the pieces around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T20:18:23-08:00","id":1424437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419691-running-scion-online-roll20-vs-astral-vs-other?p=1424391#post1424391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that's fine, but Scion really doesn't support it. Fights are narrative by design, you won't find any references to specific rules for distance, time, reach, positioning, any of that stuff. The game very literally does not care where you are on a field and largely only includes the very abstract range bands to illustrate why it might be easier to shoot a character that's narratively described as being very far away rather than trying to stab them with a sword.<br /> <br /> If you really, really want to use a map of some kind for your game, I would recommend zone maps. Rather than making a precise map of a location, just have several areas on the board that convey the general environment, any Arenas associated with each one, and how they connect to one another.<br /> <br /> So for example if you were having a divine martial arts tournament, where some of the players were competing atop bamboo poles over a bed of spikes, and some were in the stands full of screaming fans, with a cage separating them. You wouldn't map out every detail of both. Rather you would designate an &quot;Arena&quot; zone, outlined that it has the arena condition that meant that everyone had to keep balance to avoid falling onto the spikes, a &quot;Stands&quot; zone, outlined that navigating through it could be difficult given the frenzied fans, and designate that anyone trying to cross from the arena to the stands will have to deal with the cage separating the two.<br /> <br /> But obviously this can all just be extrapolated in mind's eye instead, because Divine Demigods typically don't care about something as fiddly as how many feet they move in the span of 6 seconds, they get where they're going whenever is most dramatically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>All very good points but I still maintain that there ARE tactical fights to be had. It's just that tactical in this case does not take into consideration WHERE you are in a field/zone. In this case, the tactics would be making sure that you have a target's weakness in position to take advantage of, that you use your divine powers effectively, that you're able to use fire against the Frost Giants and all that.<br /> <br /> Mostly I just wanted to make a point denoting that there's more to tactics than moving a token around on a grid. :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T05:05:07-08:00","id":1424518,"title":"","content":"They're tactical like Final Fantasy boss fights. Does the boss have Reflec up? Better cast Reflec on one of your team and start casting magic at them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T12:17:45-08:00","id":1428292,"title":"","content":"I run games for work, so I approach everything with an 'It must work, and it must not be frustrating.' mentality. I avoid all of the platforms created specifically for gaming, because I have a max capacity of 24 players (multiple groups meeting at different times) and there's always something about the gaming platforms that doesn't work for someone. Similarly, my players range from 16 to 54 (at the moment), so there's a vary wide range of technical familiarity, and I don't want that to be a barrier.<br /> <br /> I use Google Meet. There's an extension for rolling dice in the chat, you can screen share for static images, and you can share a whiteboard for maps (so people can move their own tokens). People can PM you anything they don't want the others to know about. I also use Google Sheets character sheets, because they can have the calculations done for them, and because I created a 'GM Screen' Google sheet that loads information from their character sheets for my reference.<br /> <br /> A also use Google sites for reference material that I make available to the players outside of game time. It's all Google products because they interact well, they're free, they work on everyone's system and they don't break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T22:04:44-08:00","id":1475395,"title":"","content":"Scion 2E FINALLY at Roll20 VTT platform! \u2764\ufe0f<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\"> Now Available: Polyphemus, plus Scion on roll20! &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I maybe blind - but the official Roll20 sheet do not have support for Antagonists use different stats blocks - with Dicepools, Health, etc? \ud83d\ude14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpa